    <string-array name="faq_questions">
        <item>How long does delivery take?</item>
        <item>Is the payment real?</item>
        <item>How is the delivery fee worked out?</item>
        <item>Where does FoodRush deliver?</item>
        <item>What is the delivery PIN?</item>
        <item>Can I talk to my rider?</item>
        <item>How do I use a coupon?</item>
        <item>Can I cancel an order?</item>
        <item>How do I become a rider or add my restaurant?</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="faq_answers">
        <item>The estimate is the kitchen\'s cooking time plus the quickest route on real roads, worked out with Dijkstra\'s algorithm on OpenStreetMap road data.</item>
        <item>No. Cash, bKash, Nagad, Rocket and card are demos: no money moves and no details are saved.</item>
        <item>30 tk plus 10 tk for every kilometre of road from the restaurant to you, at most 150 tk. VAT is 5% of the food.</item>
        <item>Anywhere in Bangladesh where a restaurant on FoodRush delivers. Each restaurant sets its own delivery radius.</item>
        <item>A 4-digit code on your tracking screen. Give it to the rider when the food arrives; they need it to finish the delivery.</item>
        <item>Yes. Once a rider takes your order, use Chat or Call on the tracking screen. If an internet call can\'t connect, you can call their phone instead.</item>
        <item>Enter the code in your cart and tap Apply, or tap an offer on the home screen or a restaurant page. Restaurant coupons only discount that restaurant\'s food.</item>
        <item>Yes, until the restaurant starts cooking. Use Cancel order on the tracking screen.</item>
        <item>Create a new account and choose Rider or Restaurant at sign-up. These accounts need FoodRush\'s cloud (Firebase) to be connected.</item>
    </string-array>

